 "text": "You are a credit-risk analyst at a credit-card issuer. An existing credit-card client is up for a monthly credit-line review. You must decide whether to APPROVE continued use of the credit line for the coming month or DECLINE (suspend the line).\n\nPayoffs: if you approve and the client pays, the issuer earns 3 points; if you approve and the client defaults, the issuer loses 5 points. Declining yields 0 points either way.\n\nBase rate: in about 22% of credit-card clients of this issuer, the client defaults on next month's payment.\n\nAlready known:\n- Sex (already done): it found that the client is male.\n- Recent payment activity (already done): it did not find that the client made no payment in either of the last two months while carrying a balance.\n\nYou may run any of the following checks (each at most once) before deciding.\n(A) Client age (costs 0.08 points): reports whether the client is under 25 years old.\n(B) Size of last payment (costs 0.08 points): reports whether the client's last payment covered less than 5% of the balance due.\n(C) Latest repayment status (costs 0.08 points): reports whether the client's most recent bill is two or more months overdue.\n(D) Credit limit (costs 0.15 points): reports whether the client's credit limit is NT$50,000 or less.\n(E) Marital status (costs 0.3 points): reports whether the client is single.\n(F) Latest bill payment (costs 0.15 points): reports whether the client paid the most recent bill in full and on time.\n(S) Stop and decide now (APPROVE or DECLINE).",
 "direct_prompt": "You are a credit-risk analyst at a credit-card issuer. An existing credit-card client is up for a monthly credit-line review. You must decide whether to APPROVE continued use of the credit line for the coming month or DECLINE (suspend the line).\n\nPayoffs: if you approve and the client pays, the issuer earns 3 points; if you approve and the client defaults, the issuer loses 5 points. Declining yields 0 points either way.\n\nBase rate: in about 22% of credit-card clients of this issuer, the client defaults on next month's payment.\n\nAlready known:\n- Sex (already done): it found that the client is male.\n- Recent payment activity (already done): it did not find that the client made no payment in either of the last two months while carrying a balance.\n\nYou may run any of the following checks (each at most once) before deciding.\n(A) Client age (costs 0.08 points): reports whether the client is under 25 years old.\n(B) Size of last payment (costs 0.08 points): reports whether the client's last payment covered less than 5% of the balance due.\n(C) Latest repayment status (costs 0.08 points): reports whether the client's most recent bill is two or more months overdue.\n(D) Credit limit (costs 0.15 points): reports whether the client's credit limit is NT$50,000 or less.\n(E) Marital status (costs 0.3 points): reports whether the client is single.\n(F) Latest bill payment (costs 0.15 points): reports whether the client paid the most recent bill in full and on time.\n(G) Stop and decide now (APPROVE or DECLINE).\n\nYou may run checks one at a time, see each result, and stop whenever you want.\nQuestion: What do you do next? Answer with the letter of one option only.",
